<item>
            <title>[LU-20563] OST imports stuck in NEW on ARM client nodes</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-20563</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;Recently encountered this issue at a site -&#160;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;When client reaches IDLE state, a new rpc request triggers call to ptlrpc_reconnect_if_idle() and sets state as NEW and calls ptlrpc_connect_import_locked(). &lt;br/&gt;
Most of the OST imports progresses fine from here but for some OST imports, in ptlrpc_connect_import_locked() , it goes in 3rd elseif condition and bails out from here with EALREADY and never recovers.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;code panel&quot; style=&quot;border-width: 1px;&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;codeContent panelContent&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;code-java&quot;&gt;
&lt;span class=&quot;code-keyword&quot;&gt;if&lt;/span&gt; (imp-&amp;gt;imp_state == LUSTRE_IMP_CLOSED) {
&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; spin_unlock(&amp;amp;imp-&amp;gt;imp_lock);
&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; CERROR(&lt;span class=&quot;code-quote&quot;&gt;&quot;can&apos;t connect to a closed &lt;span class=&quot;code-keyword&quot;&gt;import&lt;/span&gt;\n&quot;&lt;/span&gt;);
&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; RETURN(-EINVAL);
&#160; &#160; } &lt;span class=&quot;code-keyword&quot;&gt;else&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class=&quot;code-keyword&quot;&gt;if&lt;/span&gt; (imp-&amp;gt;imp_state == LUSTRE_IMP_FULL) {
&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; spin_unlock(&amp;amp;imp-&amp;gt;imp_lock);
&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; CERROR(&lt;span class=&quot;code-quote&quot;&gt;&quot;already connected\n&quot;&lt;/span&gt;);
&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; RETURN(0);
&#160; &#160; } &lt;span class=&quot;code-keyword&quot;&gt;else&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class=&quot;code-keyword&quot;&gt;if&lt;/span&gt; (imp-&amp;gt;imp_state == LUSTRE_IMP_CONNECTING ||
&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160;imp-&amp;gt;imp_state == LUSTRE_IMP_EVICTED ||
&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160;imp-&amp;gt;imp_connected) {           &amp;lt;------------------
&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; spin_unlock(&amp;amp;imp-&amp;gt;imp_lock);
&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; CERROR(&lt;span class=&quot;code-quote&quot;&gt;&quot;already connecting\n&quot;&lt;/span&gt;);
&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; RETURN(-EALREADY);
&#160; &#160; } &lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The investigation suggests it happens because for the problematic OST import, imp-&amp;gt;imp_connected is set.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;From code review, we see that it could happen because of an unsafe bit unset (without acquiring spinlock) of the imp_no_cached_data in another code path (introduced by &lt;a href=&quot;https://review.whamcloud.com/c/fs/lustre-release/+/43834&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;this commit&lt;/a&gt;). But this unsafe unset can mess around with other bits of the flag too.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;It is a generic race, but ARM64&#8217;s weaker ordering and different timing can make it easier to hit than x86.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
